{"id":"bf393c071d76e455","group":"58","path":"58/batch05/58-df-zfc-descriptive4-analytic-equivalence-relation.md","title":"ZFC Descriptive4 Analytic Equivalence Relation","display":"df-zfc-descriptive4-analytic-equivalence-relation — ZFC Descriptive4 Analytic Equivalence Relation","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-descriptive4-analytic-equivalence-relation","aliases":["58-df-zfc-descriptive4-analytic-equivalence-relation"],"display":"df-zfc-descriptive4-analytic-equivalence-relation — ZFC Descriptive4 Analytic Equivalence Relation","depends_on":["[[../batch17/58-df-polish-space.md]]","[[../batch14/58-df-closed-set.md]]","[[../batch02/58-df-equivalence-relation.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-descriptive4-analytic-equivalence-relation"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-descriptive4-analytic-equivalence-relation</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-descriptive4-analytic-equivalence-relation — ZFC Descriptive4 Analytic Equivalence Relation"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"4b3a8629f6a6f868\" href=\"?note=4b3a8629f6a6f868\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-polish-space.md\">../batch17/58-df-polish-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"3600401d4adbcbd4\" href=\"?note=3600401d4adbcbd4\" title=\"../batch14/58-df-closed-set.md\">../batch14/58-df-closed-set.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"908bc7b079f5d25b\" href=\"?note=908bc7b079f5d25b\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-equivalence-relation.md\">../batch02/58-df-equivalence-relation.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X,\\tau,E,\\tau_\\Pi\\in V\">\\(X,\\tau,E,\\tau_\\Pi\\in V\\)</span>, where <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_\\Pi\">\\(\\tau_\\Pi\\)</span> is the product topology on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(X\\times X)\\times\\omega^\\omega\">\\((X\\times X)\\times\\omega^\\omega\\)</span> induced by <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau\">\\(\\tau\\)</span> and the Baire topology</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Polish}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Polish}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"4b3a8629f6a6f868\" href=\"?note=4b3a8629f6a6f868\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-polish-space.md\">../batch17/58-df-polish-space.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Closed}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Closed}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"3600401d4adbcbd4\" href=\"?note=3600401d4adbcbd4\" title=\"../batch14/58-df-closed-set.md\">../batch14/58-df-closed-set.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{EquivRel}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{EquivRel}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"908bc7b079f5d25b\" href=\"?note=908bc7b079f5d25b\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-equivalence-relation.md\">../batch02/58-df-equivalence-relation.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcDescriptive4AnalyticEquivalenceRelation}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcDescriptive4AnalyticEquivalenceRelation}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}descriptive4\\text{-}analytic\\text{-}equivalence\\text{-}relation} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcDescriptive4AnalyticEquivalenceRelation}_S(X,\\tau,E)\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Polish}_S(X,\\tau)\\land\\mathrm{EquivRel}_S(E,X)\\land\n\\exists C\\subseteq(X\\times X)\\times\\omega^\\omega\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Closed}_S(C,(X\\times X)\\times\\omega^\\omega,\\tau_\\Pi)\\land\nE=\\{\\langle x,y\\rangle\\in X\\times X:\n\\exists z\\in\\omega^\\omega\\;(\\langle\\langle x,y\\rangle,z\\rangle\\in C)\\}\n\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}descriptive4\\text{-}analytic\\text{-}equivalence\\text{-}relation} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcDescriptive4AnalyticEquivalenceRelation}_S(X,\\tau,E)\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Polish}_S(X,\\tau)\\land\\mathrm{EquivRel}_S(E,X)\\land\n\\exists C\\subseteq(X\\times X)\\times\\omega^\\omega\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Closed}_S(C,(X\\times X)\\times\\omega^\\omega,\\tau_\\Pi)\\land\nE=\\{\\langle x,y\\rangle\\in X\\times X:\n\\exists z\\in\\omega^\\omega\\;(\\langle\\langle x,y\\rangle,z\\rangle\\in C)\\}\n\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Analyticity is expressed as the projection of a closed subset of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(X\\times X)\\times\\omega^\\omega\">\\((X\\times X)\\times\\omega^\\omega\\)</span>, while equivalence is checked by the registered predicate.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch17/58-df-polish-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"4b3a8629f6a6f868","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch17/58-df-polish-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch14/58-df-closed-set.md","status":"resolved","id":"3600401d4adbcbd4","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch14/58-df-closed-set.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch02/58-df-equivalence-relation.md","status":"resolve